[h1]QuickSL / Probably Stolen Tools[/h1]
Made a bad deal? Found something great you couldn't afford? Regret it the moment the customer walks out?
[b]QuickSL[/b] lets you rewind the whole pawnshop a few minutes into the past — shelves, cash, offers and customers, all of it.

[hr][/hr]

[h2]◆ Rewind[/h2]

[list]
[*][b]Customer checkpoints[/b]: a full snapshot is captured automatically after each ordinary customer's opening dialogue; double-click a checkpoint to return to that moment.
[*][b]Manual checkpoints[/b]: press F9 at any time; no customer needs to be present.
[*][b]Cross-day history[/b]: the session keeps today and yesterday; up to 20 customer/manual/closed-shop checkpoints per day, plus one free day-start anchor. Older days are released when a third day begins.
[*][b]F5 / F7[/b]: back to the previous day / back to today's opening, preferring the in-memory morning anchor. Adjacent days stay browsable after a rewind.
[*][b]F6 picker[/b]: Up/W and Down/S to move, Enter to confirm, Esc to cancel, or double-click a node. Middle/side mouse buttons can be assigned to navigation.
[*][b]Branch summaries[/b]: old nodes can be browsed without deleting the future; it is discarded only when a new branch starts, leaving up to 80 summaries.
[*][b]Leaving and returning[/b]: leaving pauses capture; returning and staying settled for ~0.5 seconds creates a node. Closed shops may keep the shutter locked overnight; OPEN/MORNING must unlock.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]◆ Chemistry assist[/h2]

[list]
[*][b]Composition and water labels[/b]: shows the main component, share, purity and grade; empty containers/seeds get proper names, and plant matter no longer takes over the main component.
[*][b]Auto-blend[/b]: dropping blendable items into a blender follows the game's own blend rules and sound; different products stay separate, and the batch is stopped early when capacity is insufficient.
[*][b]Rapid extraction[/b]: adding liquid to a container with a positive amount of alcohol converts the three mushroom-mash types into their extracts using the original ratios, rounding and conditions.
[*][b]Rapid reactions[/b]: a separate switch for only the nine explicit non-thermal reactions, with at most 512 extra steps per run and stopping as soon as nothing changes.
[*][b]Facility projections[/b]: tooltips for the water purifier, evaporator, hydroponic tray and fish tank/RAS show expected overnight output or removal, with warnings for missing water, containers or power.
[*]Every assist can be disabled independently. Automation never runs while loading, restoring or during forbidden night transitions.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]◆ Other tools[/h2]

[list]
[*][b]Quick appraisal[/b]: the inspection screen lists authenticity, issues and a suggested price, with optional auto-submit.
[*][b]Double-click to inspect[/b]: double-click an inspectable item to use a magnifying glass from your inventory, saving a drag.
[*][b]Water quality labels[/b]: water quality is labelled in real time and mismatches are highlighted in red.
[*][b]Wine labels[/b]: shows glowberry condition; unfermented bottles show expected quality, with low water reported separately.
[*][b]Dialogue fast-forward[/b]: advances ordinary customer small talk and stops at choices, SEC encounters and important dialogue.
[*][b]Multi-language[/b]: annotations read the game's native localization keys and follow the selected game language.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]◆ Settings and actions[/h2]

[list]
[*]Automatic checkpoints are on by default. When disabled, automatic morning/customer/closed/return nodes stop; manual F9, the picker and retained-node rewinds still work, while F5/F7 load a save file. Settings also has quick reload save and reroll random, both unbound by default.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]◆ Snapshot limits and diagnostics[/h2]

[list]
[*]The gear panel under Main Menu -> Mods -> Probably Stolen Tools can adjust object, field-slot and byte limits; PSTools.settings.xml can also be edited after closing the game.
[*]Higher limits allow larger checkpoints but may use more memory and cause longer pauses; below-limit graphs do not traverse extra objects.
[*]A failed capture shows the concrete exception, current limits and an actionable suggestion; logs include timing, object/slot scale and cleanup information.
[*]Settings -> View log shows the end of PSTools.log in game and copies the log path.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]◆ Save safety[/h2]

[list]
[*]The mod never calls the game's save function on its own and never modifies save files while idle.
[*]Customer/manual checkpoints are pure memory restores. F5/F7 load a copy of the checkpoint without writing the active save, and keep a [i].pre_restore[/i] backup before restore.
[*]Duplicate-history cleanup protects files waiting to be restored and files shared by other history entries; a mismatched load cancels immediately and keeps the recovery file.
[*]A manual save before the first use is still recommended, especially with many mods.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]◆ Installation and hotkeys[/h2]

[list]
[*]Click Subscribe on the Steam Workshop page, enable the mod in the game's Mods menu and restart when prompted.
[*]Load a save, enter the shop and press [b]F8[/b] to open the panel (press again to collapse).
[*]Defaults: F6 picker, F5 previous day, F7 today's opening, F8 panel, F9 manual checkpoint.
[*]All keys are rebindable: F8 -> Settings -> Hotkeys; conflicting keys are swapped automatically.
[*]For manual installation, keep both [b]ProbablyStolenTools.dll[/b] and [b]ProbablyStolenTools.StaticLayouts.dll[/b]; do not replace only the main DLL.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]◆ Compatibility[/h2]

[list]
[*]One package contains compatibility data for [b]stable 0.46D[/b] and [b]beta 1.0.0.14[/b], selected automatically at startup; future game versions still need a mod update.
[*]1.0.0.14 is still a beta; back up saves before first use. If checkpoints fail after switching back to stable, report the game version, PSTools.log and mod list.
[*]Requires only the [b]files[/b] capability and no network access; reflection-external and dynamic-code are no longer required.
[*]Generally compatible with mods that do not modify the same UI or add very large object graphs. Large saves may hit a snapshot limit; raise it in the gear panel if needed.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]◆ FAQ[/h2]

[b]Q: The customer disappeared after I rewound.[/b]
A: Rewind to a checkpoint taken [b]before[/b] the customer arrived; checkpoints are created after the dialogue ends.

[b]Q: Why is the checkpoint list shorter?[/b]
A: Browsing old nodes does not delete the future immediately; it is truncated only when the next customer starts a new branch. Leaving pauses capture, and cross-day history keeps only the adjacent two days.

[b]Q: Will this corrupt my save?[/b]
A: The mod never writes saves on its own; F5/F7 load a copy and keep .pre_restore. Still back up important progress manually.

[b]Q: Checkpoints fail after a game update.[/b]
A: Wait for a mod update and do not put DLLs from unofficial sources into Mods; include the game version and log so the cause can be identified.

[hr][/hr]

[h2]◆ Source and feedback[/h2]

This project is fully open source: [url=https://github.com/MeadalFlute/ProbablyStolenTools]github.com/MeadalFlute/ProbablyStolenTools[/url]

If something goes wrong, tell us [b]what you were doing[/b] and [b]whether you had rewound[/b], and attach the log:

[code]C:\Users\<your username>\AppData\LocalLow\Questing Goose Studio\Probably Stolen\PSTools.log[/code]

You can also open a [url=https://github.com/MeadalFlute/ProbablyStolenTools/issues]GitHub issue[/url]. Source and AGENT.md are public for adaptation.

[hr][/hr]

[b]If QuickSL helps you out, a like and a favourite go a long way — they help other players find it too.[/b]

[b]Happy trading.[/b]
